  "articles": [
    {
      "sequence_id": 1,
      "text": "Spanish often uses reflexive and indirect clitic pronouns together to indicate that something happened to someone inadvertently. Expressions like *se me cayó* mean ‘it fell on me’ (I dropped it), and *se me olvidó* means ‘it slipped my mind’. These constructions emphasise that the action was unintentional."
